{"type": "provenance", "schema": "gw2-frida-flip-sample/1", "what": "runtime probe of **flip=1 shots and multi-soldier / Bot campaign levels (18-20)**: per shot, the sampler arguments (**flip**, mode, x0/y0/step + the token stream fed in), the returned point array (ptr, n, digest, **first/last point -> sampling direction**), the `FunctionPointsEvent` assembly at 0x456810 (owner_id / start = pts[0] / end_x = pts[len-1].x) and the JSON writer 0x50eb20, and the 16 bytes the report reads (pos = pts[n-1] at execute_results 0x472865).", "why_this_gap": "every runtime sample before this round was Level 16/17 (single soldier, our side, flip=0). flip=1 (Team2 shooting towards -x) had ZERO samples, and Levels 18-20 (3/4/5 soldiers + a Bot) had none either.", "how_to_make_flip1": {"summary": "flip comes from the **team** (graphwar_turn_manager::Team::flip: Team1 x<=0 -> flip=0, Team2 x>=0 -> flip=1; docs/archive/105-team-sides.md). In campaign the player is always Team1, so our own shots are flip=0. **The Bot is Team2** => the shot the Bot fires right after ours is the flip=1 sample: enter a campaign level that HAS an opponent and just wait for its turn.", "levels_with_a_bot": "campaign level index -> docs/10-campaign.md 4: L5(bot_0), L9(bot_2), L11(bot_3), L14(bot_3), L15(bot_4), L18(bot_3), L19(bot_3), L20(bot_4)", "steps": ["user://campaign.save = \"level_20\" (unlock all 21 levels)", "main menu \"Campaign\" (534,629)", "level node #18 / #19 / #20 (1187,751) / (1429,751) / (1672,751)  [3 rows x 7 cols, snake numbering]", "popup \"Start\" (1072,1009)", "click the input box (1000,1090) -> ctrl+a -> type the expression -> long-press Fire! (1855,55) 2 s", "do NOT type the next expression immediately: the Bot takes its turn now, and ITS shot is the flip=1 sample (x0 > 0, points run towards -x, owner_id = the Bot soldier)"], "ui_check": "in Levels 18-20 the prompt reads `dy/dx =` (func=1, DiffEq); the Bot fires by itself."}, "build": {"game": "Graphwar II Linux 2.0.60 (Steam)", "libgraphwarrust.so_sha256": "9a53811518e74b7575c1b9dd1f21cdd1f4f015bfdcd8eaeee4dfdf0bcabed187", "engine": "Godot 4.7.stable.official + godot-rust (API v4.6, runtime v4.7)", "address_space": "RVA = ELF virtual address = module offset; Ghidra address = RVA + 0x100000", "hooked_rva": {"sampler_calculate": "0x3c2530", "evaluate": "0x4eb9d0", "execute_results": "0x472470", "exec_queue_probe": "0x4724cc", "pos_read_movdqu": "0x472865", "slot_9bac98": "0x9bac98", "fnpoints_ctor": "0x456810", "fnpoints_ser_json": "0x50eb20"}}, "how": {"harness": "Xvfb :93 -screen 0 1920x1160x24 -listen tcp -ac (+ mesa-only EGL/GLX env)", "driver": "tools/frida_flip_probe.py --attach (NOT frida spawn: spawn hangs the game in wait4)", "probe": "tools/frida_flip_probe.js (read-only Interceptor hooks; no memory writes)", "sampler_abi": "0x3c2530 (out: Vec<(f64,f64)> = rdi, tokens: &TokenBuf{cap,ptr,len} = rsi, FLIP = edx, MODE = ecx [0=Normal, 1=Ode], x0 = xmm0, y0 = xmm1, step = xmm2). Read off the prologue; 0x3c25a4 `test %bpl,%bpl` is the flip branch.", "fnpoints_abi": "0x456810: rdi=self, esi=owner_id (u32), rdx=&Vec<(f64,f64)>; the body reads pts[len-1].x (0x4569b8) -> end_x and pts[0] (0x4569be) -> start_x/start_y. 0x50eb20 writes them into the JSON: rsi=&event{start_x@0,start_y@8,end_x@0x10,owner_id@0x18}.", "digest": "FNV-1a 64 over ALL 16*n bytes (`digest_xy`) and over the y halves only (`digest_y`), computed INSIDE the game process at the moment of the call (probe `digestOf`).", "array_digest_spec": {"bytes": "one point array = 16*n bytes: 8 bytes of x (little-endian f64) + 8 bytes of y (little-endian f64), in point order", "sha256": "SHA-256 over exactly those 16*n bytes, computed by the driver from the probe's `arr.hex` when the sample is extracted (whole arrays are NOT committed)", "fnv": "FNV-1a-64 over the same 16*n bytes (`digest_xy`) / over the y halves only (`digest_y`)", "verify": "re-run the driver with `--full-array`, take `arr.hex`, sha256 it — it must equal `arr.sha256` here; the driver ALSO recomputes FNV from the same bytes and compares with the probe-time digest (`arr.digest_selfcheck`)"}, "positive_control": "probe self-test at install: two 100-point synthetic arrays -> same; flip 1 bit at point 37 -> diffPoints=1; flip one more at point 90 -> 2. Runtime: flip=0 and flip=1 shots of the same match produce opposite array directions and different digests, so the comparison code does report differences on real data."}, "cut": "per shot: expression typed (host marker + marker_dt_ms), flip/mode/x0/y0/step, the token stream fed to the sampler ({tag, value-bits}), the array the report reads (ptr, n, digest, first/last/second-last point), the derived sampling direction (`arr_dir`) and x0 sign, the other sampler calls of the same shot, the `FunctionPoints` assembly + JSON writer, the execute_results queue snapshot, and the 16 bytes read by the `movdqu` (pos_x/pos_y).", "dropped": "beat rows, whole-array hex, and every evaluator sample except the first few.", "no_local_paths": "no filesystem path and no user name; pointers are ASLR-random per run.", "sources": [{"label": "l05_normal", "raw_jsonl_sha256": "3c8b1a039add10f26316f0bf87b8479896a844bc9237a44430f6e6d608731a32", "raw_jsonl_lines": 389, "records_by_type": {"cfg_ack": 1, "selftest": 1, "hooks": 1, "beat": 34, "marker": 2, "calc": 326, "fnpoints_ctor": 8, "fnpoints": 4, "exec_enter": 4, "exec_queue": 4, "pos_read": 4}, "shots": 4}], "probe_selftest_at_install": {"identical_reports_same": true, "onebit_reports_diff": true, "twobit_reports_diff": true, "detail": {"same": true, "one": 1, "two": 2}}, "hooks": {"type": "hooks", "base": "7f30bae00000", "size": 10241312, "hooks": [{"name": "sampler", "rva": "0x3c2530"}, {"name": "evaluate", "rva": "0x4eb9d0"}, {"name": "execute_results", "rva": "0x472470"}, {"name": "exec_queue", "rva": "0x4724cc"}, {"name": "pos_read", "rva": "0x472865"}, {"name": "fnpoints_ctor", "rva": "0x456810"}, {"name": "fnpoints_ser", "rva": "0x50eb20"}], "slot_sampler": {"addr": "7f30bb7bac98", "raw": "30251cbb307f0000200c26bb307f0000", "target": "7f30bb1c2530", "target_rva": "gw+3c2530"}}, "counts": {"shots": 4, "distinct_modes": [0], "distinct_flips": [0, 1], "shots_by_flip": {"0": 2, "1": 2}, "array_direction_by_flip": {"x_increasing|flip=0": 2, "x_decreasing|flip=1": 2}, "pos_read_with_n": 4, "pos_bytes_equal_array_last_point": 2, "arr_truncated_shots": 2, "digest_selfcheck_ok": 4, "digest_selfcheck_total": 4, "pos_ptr_is_one_of_our_calc_calls": 2, "flip1_x_decreasing": 2, "flip1_shots": 2, "flip0_x_increasing": 2, "flip0_shots": 2, "flip1_x0_positive": 2, "flip0_x0_negative": 2, "wire_end_x_eq_pos_x": 4, "wire_start_eq_shooter_x0": 4, "owner_ids_seen": [230, 231, 233, 234]}, "notes": ["战役 Level 5（关 6）：func=0（Normal）、2 士兵、1 个 Bot（bot_0）、有散布障碍。Normal 局的 token 流里带修正常数，所以这个文件专门用来答 dispatch/49 的 ①（修正量取号）：4 发里 2 发我方 flip=0、2 发 Bot 的 flip=1。"]}
